// Expected: a0 at one session and at two.
//
// A matching run of the same agent is not an attack, whatever its session
// index. Alice sends an authenticated challenge; the attacker routes it to
// Bob#2 rather than Bob, and routes Bob#2's answer back to Alice. Bob#2 is
// another run of the same Bob, with the same peer binding, and it computes
// MAC(k, CONCAT(na, nb#2)) itself: the attacker never learns k, forges
// nothing, and no Bob send is accepted twice. Alice's acceptance has exactly
// one matching Bob run, so injective agreement holds and the query must pass
// at both session counts.
//
// The counterweight is session_replay_breaks_injectivity.vp, where the value
// delivered is a sibling run's own honest output, which its own partner also
// accepts: one send, two acceptances, a1.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	knows private k
	generates na
	t1 = MAC(k, na)
]

Alice -> Bob: na, t1

principal Bob[
	knows private k
	_ = ASSERT(t1, MAC(k, na))?
	generates nb
	m2 = MAC(k, CONCAT(na, nb))
]

Bob -> Alice: nb, m2

principal Alice[
	_ = ASSERT(m2, MAC(k, CONCAT(na, nb)))?
]

queries[
	authentication? Bob -> Alice: m2
]
